From: MyWirelessAndroidAutoDongle contributors
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: accessory: pass HID buffer size on Linux 6.12.114

The selected compatibility candidate has the six-argument HID raw-event API.
The shared accessory backport still calls the older five-argument API and
fails to compile against that candidate.

Bound both the readable buffer and the report data to the completed USB
request length. This does not claim any unreceived bytes are available.

Apply after the two existing shared accessory patches, only for the pinned
Radxa kernel candidate. Existing Pi source pins and patches stay unchanged.

Source: https://github.com/gregkh/linux/blob/85d82e0d7c2dfd3e75d34f35b7ebbf41f45c9c4e/drivers/hid/hid-core.c
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_accessory.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_accessory.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_accessory.c
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_accessory.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_accessory.c
@@ -501,7 +501,8 @@ static void acc_complete_send_hid_event(struct usb_ep *ep,
 		return;
 	}
 
-	hid_report_raw_event(hid->hid, HID_INPUT_REPORT, req->buf, length, 1);
+	hid_report_raw_event(hid->hid, HID_INPUT_REPORT, req->buf,
+			     length, length, 1);
 }
 
 static int acc_hid_parse(struct hid_device *hid)
